Conceptual lineage
------------------

Replay cursors, OHLC-style fill models, and splitting rule checks into
engine-enforced versus read-only assessment are ideas this project
inherits conceptually from CandleDrill, also by KINFX / Kinfxhk:

https://github.com/Kinfxhk/candledrill

CandleDrill is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License,
version 3 or later (AGPL-3.0-or-later). perpsdrill is a separate work.
It does not copy CandleDrill's interface, palette, or futures contract
model, and it is not a release of that repository.

The teaching liquidation, slippage gate, and replay in this tree are
original. They are an isolated approximation for practice. They are not
CandleDrill's fill model, and they are not an exchange's closed-form
liquidation price.

Synthetic practice data
-----------------------

SYNTH-IDX1, SYNTH-METAL1, SYNTH-IDX2 and SYNTH-BTC are fictional practice
ids. The seeded generator runs locally without a market-data feed. Its
price, tick and volatility settings are teaching assumptions. This is
synthetic practice only: not an index-licensed product, not exchange, CME,
or Nasdaq data, and not a futures contract specification. perpsdrill is
not affiliated with, endorsed by, or licensed by any exchange or index
provider. SYNTH-BTC is a separate Bitcoin-like fictional profile, not an
exchange feed or a record of Bitcoin prices. No exchange logos or
endorsement are implied. Third-party market data has its own terms; the
source-code license does not relicense that data.

Live market data
----------------

Live klines are fetched on demand, in the browser, from Binance's public
data endpoint (data-api.binance.vision) and attributed on the desk. No
market data is bundled or redistributed in this repository.

No affiliation
--------------

perpdrill is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or a client of any
